1. THE "PLEASE DON'T STEAL IT" CLAUSE

You may modify the source code for personal or educational purposes.

You may learn from it.

You may stare at it for several hours wondering why changing one line somehow broke seventeen unrelated systems.

You may NOT copy the entire project, change the title, replace the logo, and proudly announce:

"Guys, I made a game."

That is not software development.
That is Ctrl+C with ambition.

2. THE BUG OWNERSHIP ACT

All bugs discovered in the original Game are officially classified as:

"Unexpected gameplay features."

If you modify the Game and introduce additional bugs, those bugs legally, spiritually, and emotionally belong to you.

The original developers refuse custody.

3. THE "IT WORKS ON MY MACHINE" PROVISION

If the Game works correctly on the developers' computers but fails to run on yours, the developers reserve the right to respond:

"Interesting. It works on my machine."

This statement shall constitute a complete technical investigation.

Further debugging may occur eventually.

No promises.

4. SOURCE CODE WARNING

Parts of this software may contain:

- questionable variable names,
- TODO comments older than some civilizations,
- code nobody remembers writing,
- temporary solutions that became permanent,
- functions that work for reasons unknown to modern science,
- and at least one line that MUST NOT BE TOUCHED.

If you encounter code accompanied by comments such as:

// DO NOT DELETE THIS

or

// somehow this fixes it

you are strongly advised to respect the ancient knowledge.

5. WARRANTY

THE GAME IS PROVIDED "AS IS."

Actually, sometimes it isn't even provided "as is."

Sometimes it is provided "as we last managed to get it working."

No warranty is provided that the Game will:

- run,
- launch,
- save,
- load,
- maintain a stable frame rate,
- respect the laws of physics,
- respect the laws of mathematics,
- or continue functioning after a Unity update.

6. DAMAGE AND LIABILITY

The developers shall not be held responsible for:

lost save files,
corrupted projects,
unexpected crashes,
NPCs walking through walls,
characters achieving low Earth orbit,
bosses becoming immortal,
missing textures,
audio playing at 400% volume,
or computers developing emotional problems.

Use at your own risk.

7. STACK OVERFLOW / INTERNET CLAUSE

Any resemblance between certain pieces of code and solutions found somewhere on the internet is purely coincidental, educational, inspirational, traditional, inevitable, and absolutely none of your business.

8. THE 3 A.M. DEVELOPMENT EXCEPTION

Code written after 03:00 local time is exempt from normal standards of readability, logic, architecture, mathematics, naming conventions, and human dignity.

Such code shall be considered valid if:

a) it compiles, or

b) nobody touches it.

9. MODIFICATION RIGHTS

You are allowed to create modifications, experiments, forks, and personal versions of the Game.

However, if your modification somehow becomes significantly better than the original Game, the developers reserve the right to:

a) pretend they always planned that feature,

b) inspect your code with uncomfortable interest,

and

c) quietly reconsider their career choices.

10. COMMERCIAL USE

Commercial redistribution of the complete Game or substantial portions of it without explicit permission is prohibited.

Selling an unchanged copy for €79.99 and calling it the "Ultimate Definitive Remastered GOTY Edition" does not magically make it your intellectual property.

Nice attempt.

11. FINAL LEGAL DECLARATION

By using, compiling, modifying, launching, downloading, cloning, forking, observing, thinking about, or standing suspiciously close to this repository, you acknowledge that software development is an inherently unstable activity performed by humans who voluntarily turn coffee into error messages.

If everything works:

Excellent.

If something breaks:

Check the console.

If the console contains 47 red errors:

Check the first one.

If fixing the first one creates 83 new errors:

Welcome to game development.

